<title>UK: UK Labour's Brown says would be tough on spending.</title>
<headline>UK Labour's Brown says would be tough on spending.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British opposition Labour party finance spokesman Gordon Brown said on Monday he would place &quot;tough controls&quot; on public spending if his party were to win the next election.  </p>
<p>&quot;I can't allow public spending to get out of control and I will not do so,&quot; Brown told BBC radio. &quot;No credible chancellor would do anything other than what I will do. I'm going to have tough controls on public spending.&quot;</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 6784</p>
</text>
